#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105478 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105701 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c9317eb-d1ce-5f42-b69b-a37e643b865b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Projection Using Angle and Magnitude"}] :question/id #uuid "3278333b-a29e-54c5-bc94-b5525bc6f751" :question/math-academy-id "e-14617" :question/problem "Suppose that $|\\,\\mathbf{a}\\,|=8,|\\,\\mathbf{b}\\,|=4$ and that the angle between the vectors is $\\theta = \\dfrac{5\\pi}{6}.$ Find the vector projection of $\\mathbf{a}$ onto $\\mathbf{b}$ in terms of the vector $\\mathbf{b}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the scalar projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a & =|\\,a\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =8\\cdot (-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\  & =-4\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the unit vector that is parallel to $\\mathbf{b}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{u} = \\dfrac{\\mathbf{b}}{|\\,\\mathbf{b}\\,|} = \\dfrac{\\mathbf{b}}{4} = \\dfrac{1}{4} \\mathbf{b}\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the vector projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & ={\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a\\cdot u \\\\  & =-4\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}b \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{3}b\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105479 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105702 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0670172-77cb-5e88-b78d-e5136c06095f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Projection Using Components"}] :question/id #uuid "58b2269d-f998-5ba5-9df8-54ea422c43aa" :question/math-academy-id "e-14618" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 1,-3,5 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 5,-4,0 \\rangle$. Find the vector projection of $\\mathbf{a}$ onto $\\mathbf{b}$." :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 5+(-3)\\cdot (-4)+5\\cdot 0}{{5}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{0}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{41}⟨5,-4,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{85}{41},-\\frac{68}{41},0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105480 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105703 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "84c96375-27d5-5ada-a952-34e09b3e92bf" :knowledge-point/title "Perpendicular Vectors"}] :question/id #uuid "663f3f5e-56cf-5517-ba1e-d1a355767e0b" :question/math-academy-id "e-14619" :question/problem "Let ![](images/e1/e199e48633dbaeeb817da846163a9c8a9bf1ae3355c69b56461b25a13ef73406.png) and ![](images/4c/4ce6e454ff96976ddeb735d1ab42562fe3b7eb16f16e7c0402d8040f9586907b.png). Find the vector projection of $\\mathbf{a}$ onto $\\mathbf{b}$." :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 1+0\\cdot 5+1\\cdot (-1)}{{1}^{2}+{5}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{{1}^{2}+{5}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}b \\\\  & =⟨0,0,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290297 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105703 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "84c96375-27d5-5ada-a952-34e09b3e92bf" :knowledge-point/title "Perpendicular Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c7ef318-2fcb-5abc-8a64-d58156e31752" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288215} {:answer/id #uuid "5c11b723-d398-54b7-a85d-9a83c61b10d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288673} {:answer/id #uuid "5dc7f785-7e44-5d1c-b5f4-fda66276cfbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288688} {:answer/id #uuid "9955ee51-0d6d-5dfb-98be-feb9ccd48fbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289058} {:answer/id #uuid "d81110dc-6d84-5507-8cfa-a7555e54190e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289470}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c11b723-d398-54b7-a85d-9a83c61b10d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288673} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c5922bf-d851-5e5c-8bcd-35ace642db54" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290040}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6c452b5c-8f3c-5759-a6a2-00c200b73978" :question/math-academy-id "q-212462" :question/problem "Let $a=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ x\\end{aligned}].$ Given that the projection of $a$ onto $b$ is the zero vector, find the value of $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Since $a$ is a nonzero vector, its projection onto another nonzero vector $b$ equals the zero vector only when the vectors are perpendicular. \n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\na⊥b\\,⟹\\,a\\cdot b=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y}+{a}_{z}\\cdot {b}_{z} \\\\  & =1\\cdot 1+3\\cdot (-2)+2\\cdot x \\\\  & =2x-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ 2x-5 & =0 \\\\ 2x & =5 \\\\ x & =\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186374538 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105703 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "84c96375-27d5-5ada-a952-34e09b3e92bf" :knowledge-point/title "Perpendicular Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10a6363d-50b7-53ee-9211-bf98b3b730c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374540} {:answer/id #uuid "6d50033c-ac1e-5bc6-84ee-1d4b187400c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374541} {:answer/id #uuid "2c9d11de-00b2-5f81-bbb0-9e2cfe2d24d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374542} {:answer/id #uuid "4f93f9db-ba0a-508a-846f-8f31e1eda3c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374543} {:answer/id #uuid "4bade5c1-6626-584d-87f1-ee5499c60e01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374544}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f93f9db-ba0a-508a-846f-8f31e1eda3c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374543} :answer-field/id #uuid "af73e53b-f8ec-53d4-ad2f-688f3fcd26ab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374539}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cfdc0ea6-159a-5bd6-ad02-2e0fd2db5b29" :question/math-academy-id "q-212464" :question/problem "Let $a=[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ x \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].$ Given that the projection of $a$ onto $b$ is the zero vector, find the value of $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Since $a$ is a nonzero vector, its projection onto another nonzero vector $b$ equals the zero vector only when the vectors are perpendicular. \n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\na⊥b\\,⟹\\,a\\cdot b=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y}+{a}_{z}\\cdot {b}_{z} \\\\  & =-6\\cdot (-2)+(-3)\\cdot x+0\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =12-3x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ 12-3x & =0 \\\\ -3x & =-12 \\\\ x & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299634 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105702 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0670172-77cb-5e88-b78d-e5136c06095f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Projection Using Components"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e9d61422-1475-5621-ad7d-a849aaca114f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298546}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e9d61422-1475-5621-ad7d-a849aaca114f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298546} :answer-field/id #uuid "0984c5b8-6bfe-56e8-9582-60026aa3bd96" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298667} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c9f7fec6-5215-539e-8f83-5634b3c4076a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{34}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298431}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c9f7fec6-5215-539e-8f83-5634b3c4076a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{34}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298431} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e38d24f-0d2e-5b55-b975-90a7ef2d3a53" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298686} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24aadbe1-8097-598a-9d4b-d9e79efcd1e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{17}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297709}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "24aadbe1-8097-598a-9d4b-d9e79efcd1e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{17}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297709} :answer-field/id #uuid "9689e94a-473b-55d0-80de-83ad1a852f62" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299134}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0810600b-ad06-5852-ade5-064bb8170efd" :question/math-academy-id "q-317655" :question/problem "Let $r=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]$ and $s=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$ Find the vector projection of $r$ onto $s.$\n\n${\\text{proj}}_{s}\\,r=⟨$ \n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$,$\n{{field-3}}\n$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{s}\\,r & =\\frac{r\\cdot s}{s\\cdot s}s \\\\  & =\\frac{{r}_{x}{s}_{x}+{r}_{y}{s}_{y}+{r}_{z}{s}_{z}}{{s}_{x}^{2}+{s}_{y}^{2}+{s}_{z}^{2}}s \\\\  & =\\frac{(-3)\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 0+7\\cdot (-2)}{{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}s \\\\  & =\\frac{-17}{5}⟨1,0,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\,-\\frac{17}{5},0,\\frac{34}{5}\\,⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299636 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105702 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0670172-77cb-5e88-b78d-e5136c06095f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Projection Using Components"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "406c9253-8200-5ad3-8d4b-33726202a988" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{23}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297809}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "406c9253-8200-5ad3-8d4b-33726202a988" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{23}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297809} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d8666c5-0963-50a4-bc97-4b5c38053501" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298959} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1df406d7-a2cd-566a-9e5c-dbf376476be5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{23}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297681}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1df406d7-a2cd-566a-9e5c-dbf376476be5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{23}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297681} :answer-field/id #uuid "d08d1232-d14d-502d-8d1a-ea40bec46176" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299341} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "74ad9205-623c-5b5c-8b1b-874ef60380c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{23}{30}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298055}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74ad9205-623c-5b5c-8b1b-874ef60380c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{23}{30}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298055} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9147c73-f105-5d8b-83ed-2692f2208968" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299426}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1656678a-52ed-5990-af8d-fd8bfe8d48c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-317658" :question/problem "Let $c=⟨-2,1,5⟩$ and $d=⟨4,0,-3⟩.$ Find the vector projection of $d$ onto $c.$\n\n${\\text{proj}}_{c}\\,d=⟨$\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$,$\n{{field-3}}\n$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{c}\\,d & =\\frac{c\\cdot d}{c\\cdot c}c \\\\  & =\\frac{{c}_{x}{d}_{x}+{c}_{y}{d}_{y}+{c}_{z}{d}_{z}}{{c}_{x}^{2}+{c}_{y}^{2}+{c}_{z}^{2}}c \\\\  & =\\frac{(-2)\\cdot 4+1\\cdot 0+5\\cdot (-3)}{(-2)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{5}^{2}}c \\\\  & =\\frac{-8+0-15}{4+1+25}⟨-2,1,5⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{-23}{30}⟨-2,1,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\,\\frac{23}{15},-\\frac{23}{30},-\\frac{23}{6}\\,⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299663 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105703 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "84c96375-27d5-5ada-a952-34e09b3e92bf" :knowledge-point/title "Perpendicular Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fa759f3a-59cf-57f1-9eb4-fe076883ee65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298620}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa759f3a-59cf-57f1-9eb4-fe076883ee65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298620} :answer-field/id #uuid "415cdd53-3c35-5e12-a9ad-bdb260275079" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298863}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2940b787-7de0-58e6-a5d9-3477f08d2d69" :question/math-academy-id "q-317944" :question/problem "Let $a=t\\,i-4j+k$ and $b=4i+j.$ Given that the projection of $a$ onto $b$ is the zero vector, find the value of $t.$\n\n$t=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since $a$ is a nonzero vector, its projection onto another nonzero vector $b$ equals the zero vector only when the vectors are perpendicular.\n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\na⊥b\\,⟹\\,a\\cdot b=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y}+{a}_{z}\\cdot {b}_{z} \\\\  & =t\\cdot 4+(-4)\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =4t-4+0 \\\\  & =4t-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ 4t-4 & =0 \\\\ 4t & =4 \\\\ t & =1 \\\\ t & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106480 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105701 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c9317eb-d1ce-5f42-b69b-a37e643b865b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Projection Using Angle and Magnitude"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c46506b-71f4-5dd4-8073-f478001468d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186105029} {:answer/id #uuid "aa28895b-01c4-5a6a-8497-a8805ff0c18e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186105030} {:answer/id #uuid "0bd413b9-0ccc-5243-898a-0e04480488f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186105031} {:answer/id #uuid "371bec7c-71dd-546e-8bff-407c6e758672" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186105032} {:answer/id #uuid "7c124655-5867-56b0-ab0d-79de478b24e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186105033}] :answer-field/id #uuid "295493ed-d510-566e-997d-2641481e7989" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186105028}] :question/id #uuid "e48c0a41-451d-5386-8afe-32a1dfe30bdb" :question/math-academy-id "q-71836" :question/problem "Suppose that $\\mid c|= 12$, $\\mid d|= 6$ and that the angle between the vectors is $θ = \\frac{2π}{3}$. Find the vector projection of $d$ onto $c$ in terms of the vector $c$."}]}
